WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.865 --> 00:00:17.396
One spring day Robin Hood was watching Little John repair a bow.

2
00:00:18.197 --> 00:00:21.940
The day was warm and pleasant, and Robin felt very content.

3
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.624
"I'd rather live here than in the king's palace," announced Robin.

4
00:00:26.644 --> 00:00:29.586
"The woods are green and beautiful.

5
00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:31.208
Flowers are blooming.

6
00:00:32.112 --> 00:00:33.953
We have plenty of food and fresh water.

7
00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:38.555
There's no better place than Sherwood Forest in springtime."

8
00:00:38.575 --> 00:00:44.878
"Yes, I'm very happy with our life," agreed Little John.

9
00:00:45.518 --> 00:00:47.979
He rubbed the string of his bow with some wax.

10
00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:53.761
"You mentioned spring, Robin, but actually, every season has its rewards.

11
00:00:54.282 --> 00:00:54.922
Even winter.

12
00:00:55.502 --> 00:00:59.404
Do you remember the winter day we spent with that friar and two beggars?

13
00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:06.783
The friar seemed to be enjoying himself, strolling around the countryside, finding both good food and a warm

14
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:11.785
fire. If I couldn't live here in Sherwood Forest, I'd like to be a friar."

15
00:01:13.126 --> 00:01:14.546
"Really?" said Robin.

16
00:01:14.566 --> 00:01:16.347
"I'd choose to be a beggar.

17
00:01:16.887 --> 00:01:19.148
I thought those two beggars led a happier life.

18
00:01:19.728 --> 00:01:22.910
They told such wonderful stories about meeting people."

19
00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.531
Suddenly Robin had an idea.

20
00:01:25.551 --> 00:01:27.732
"Let's have an adventure today!

21
00:01:28.328 --> 00:01:30.949
I'll try begging while you try a friar's life.

22
00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:33.490
And then we'll see who has the most fun."

23
00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:35.991
Little John laid down his bow.

24
00:01:36.011 --> 00:01:37.452
"Let's do that!"

25
00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:42.694
Robin and his band kept a chest filled with all kinds of clothes.

26
00:01:43.314 --> 00:01:46.596
Little John pulled out a gray friar's robe and put it on.

27
00:01:48.056 --> 00:01:49.617
He tied a string of beads.

28
00:01:50.538 --> 00:01:52.879
Then he went to show Robin and the other men.

29
00:01:53.559 --> 00:01:55.560
Everyone roared with laughter.

30
00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:02.142
The robe was way too short, but Little John didn't care.

31
00:02:03.563 --> 00:02:06.765
He folded his hands in prayer and stared at the ground.

32
00:02:06.785 --> 00:02:10.167
"Do you think I could pass for a humble friar?"

33
00:02:10.187 --> 00:02:14.329
"Never!" Friar Tuck laughed.

34
00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:20.653
"You must look people in the eye, or they'll suspect you're a fraud."

35
00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:26.496
"At least he has a costume," said Robin.

36
00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.703
"I'll have to buy clothes from the first beggar I see."

37
00:02:32.264 --> 00:02:36.187
The two men picked up their staffs and set off in different directions.

38
00:02:37.288 --> 00:02:40.070
Little John walked along, whistling happily.

39
00:02:41.151 --> 00:02:45.455
Birds twittered in the trees and green hills rose toward the sky.

40
00:02:46.636 --> 00:02:50.679
Little John soon met three pretty girls, carrying eggs to market.

41
00:02:50.699 --> 00:02:56.524
"Oh, you shouldn't have to carry those heavy baskets," said Little John.

42
00:02:57.108 --> 00:02:58.128
"Let me help you."

43
00:02:58.148 --> 00:03:01.089
"How will you manage all three baskets?"

44
00:03:01.509 --> 00:03:02.470
asked the first girl.

45
00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.050
"Like this!"

46
00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.551
Little John handed his staff to the second girl.

47
00:03:08.131 --> 00:03:13.013
Then he tied one basket to his back and carried the other two in his hands.

48
00:03:14.813 --> 00:03:16.834
The girls blushed and giggled.

49
00:03:19.035 --> 00:03:23.056
As the four of them walked toward Nottingham, they made an amusing sight.

50
00:03:23.992 --> 00:03:27.995
Here were three pretty girls with a huge friar in a short robe.

51
00:03:28.536 --> 00:03:31.738
The friar was trying not to drop three baskets of eggs.

52
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.322
People joked with Little John, and he joked right back.

53
00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.905
He laughed and talked with the three girls.

54
00:03:39.925 --> 00:03:42.667
"I'm having a great day!"

55
00:03:42.987 --> 00:03:43.988
he said to himself.

56
00:03:44.769 --> 00:03:47.811
Little John felt sad when they reached the edge of town.

57
00:03:47.831 --> 00:03:51.194
"I must leave you here," he said.

58
00:03:51.914 --> 00:03:55.785
He didn't dare to enter town—he might meet the sheriff's men!

59
00:03:59.227 --> 00:04:02.950
Little John walked along by himself and reached a little building.

60
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.572
A sign hung out front with a picture of a stag's head.

61
00:04:06.592 --> 00:04:08.634
"I'm thirsty," he thought.

62
00:04:08.654 --> 00:04:10.475
"And that's an inn."

63
00:04:11.816 --> 00:04:15.999
A beggar and a peddler sat outside the inn, having something to drink.

64
00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:18.400
Two horses were tied to a tree.

65
00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:21.582
"Are those your horses?"

66
00:04:22.003 --> 00:04:22.883
asked Little John.

67
00:04:22.903 --> 00:04:28.242
"No, they belong to two friars, who are inside eating.

68
00:04:28.802 --> 00:04:30.863
Would you like to share our drink?"

69
00:04:31.223 --> 00:04:31.963
asked the beggar.

70
00:04:31.983 --> 00:04:33.604
"Oh, yes!

71
00:04:34.144 --> 00:04:37.245
I've been walking all morning and I'm quite thirsty."

72
00:04:38.526 --> 00:04:41.627
Little John enjoyed a drink and then began to sing.

73
00:04:43.268 --> 00:04:45.609
Soon the two friars came out of the inn.

74
00:04:46.329 --> 00:04:50.271
One friar was tall and thin, and the other was short and fat.

75
00:04:50.991 --> 00:04:54.265
When they heard Little John singing, they both frowned.

76
00:04:54.285 --> 00:05:00.448
"That's not a proper song for a friar to sing," scolded the tall friar.

77
00:05:00.468 --> 00:05:03.350
"You're a disgrace to friars everywhere."

78
00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:06.592
"You know who's a disgrace?"

79
00:05:07.052 --> 00:05:07.953
said Little John.

80
00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:10.494
"Friars who cheat the poor."

81
00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:15.097
The beggar and peddler laughed, but the two friars scowled.

82
00:05:15.837 --> 00:05:22.048
As the friars walked toward their horses, Little John offered to help them mount.

83
00:05:22.068 --> 00:05:24.110
"We don't need your help," said the tall friar.

84
00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.311
"Go away!"

85
00:05:25.331 --> 00:05:27.792
"Oh, no," said Little John.

86
00:05:27.812 --> 00:05:32.395
"I'm sorry that you don't like my company, but I'm a friar too.

87
00:05:32.956 --> 00:05:34.517
So I'm coming with you."

88
00:05:35.297 --> 00:05:42.522
The beggar and peddler grinned at the sight—a tall friar in a short robe rushing after two scowling
